{"id":"s3.6.3","slug":"integration","title":"Integration","content":"<p class=\"mb-4\">Integration problems on the test are typically basic definite integrals of polynomials. Integration is the reverse of differentiation (the anti-derivative). For a term $ax^n$, its integral is $\\frac{a}{n+1}x^{n+1}$.</p><p class=\"mb-4\">To evaluate a definite integral $\\int_a^b f(x)dx$, you find the anti-derivative $F(x)$ and then compute $F(b) - F(a)$.</p><p class=\"mb-4\">A key shortcut: The integral of an odd function over a symmetric interval $[-a, a]$ is always zero. For example, $\\int_{-\\pi/4}^{\\pi/4} \\sin(x) dx = 0$ because sin(x) is an odd function.</p>","summary":"Integration problems on the test are typically basic definite integrals of polynomials.","generation_guideline":"Generate a problem asking to evaluate a definite integral of a simple polynomial.","questions":[{"id":1,"text":"Calculate $\\int_0^2 (x^2 + 3) dx$. (mixed number)","answer":"8 2/3","kind":"exact","requiredForm":"mixed","tags":["bases","calculus"]},{"id":2,"text":"Calculate $\\int_2^4 (2x - 3) dx$.","answer":"6","kind":"exact","tags":["bases","calculus"]},{"id":3,"text":"Calculate $\\int_1^4 2x dx$.","answer":"15","kind":"exact","tags":["bases","calculus"]},{"id":4,"text":"Calculate $\\int_{-3}^3 x^2 dx$.","answer":"18","kind":"exact","tags":["calculus"]},{"id":5,"text":"Calculate $\\int_0^4 \\frac{x}{2} dx$.","answer":"4","kind":"exact","tags":["fractions","bases","calculus"]},{"id":6,"text":"Calculate $\\int_0^1 \\frac{x^3}{4} dx$.","answer":"1/16","kind":"exact","tags":["fractions","bases","calculus"]},{"id":7,"text":"Calculate $\\int_1^3 (x^2 - 2) dx$. (mixed number)","answer":"4 2/3","kind":"exact","requiredForm":"mixed","tags":["bases","calculus"]},{"id":8,"text":"Calculate $\\int_{-2}^4 (x + 1) dx$.","answer":"12","kind":"exact","tags":["calculus"]},{"id":9,"text":"Calculate $\\int_0^\\pi \\sin(x) dx$.","answer":"2","kind":"exact","tags":["bases","trigonometry","calculus"]},{"id":10,"text"